   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to implementing a\nresidential parking system in the village of Croton-on-Hudson",
    "basePrintNo": "S7740",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7740-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1640-q, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7740\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to implementing\na residential parking system in the village of Croton-on-Hudson\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation to implement a residential parking\nsystem in the Village of Croton-on-Hudson.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. A new section 1640-q is added to the Vehicle and Traffic Law,\nand establishes a residential parking system in the village of Croton-\non-Hudson.\n\n1. The Croton-on-Hudson Village Board of Trustees may provide for a\nresidential parking permit system.\n\n2. Such residential parking permit system may only be established on\nboth sides of Young and Hastings Avenues within the Village of Croton-\non-Hudson.\n\n3. No permit shall be required on streets or portions of streets where\nthe adjacent properties are zoned commercial/retail use.\n\n4. Establishes what the local residential parking system law or ordi-\nnance shall include.\n\n5. No ordinance shall be adopted until a public hearing has occurred.\n\nSection 2. Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nThis portion of this memorandum is not applicable at this time.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation was requested by the Village of Croton-on-Hudson to\naddress non-residents circumventing the parking fee at the Croton-Harmon\nTrain Station's commuter parking lot, and parking instead on Hastings\nand Young Avenues. Residents have requested this parking system as a way\nto address their concerns, which include driveways being blocked, visi-\nbility being limited due to 'over-crowding', and the reduction of park-\ning for the residents themselves and their guests.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is new legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nThere are no fiscal implications associated with the passage of this\nlegislation.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis legislation shall take effect immediately.\n",
